# Papers are FETCHED, not committed — same pattern as `fetch-lean-seed.sh`.
#
# WHY: 41 papers is 76 MB against a .git that is already 1.7 GB, and every one of
# them is a published paper anyone can re-download. What must be reproducible is
# WHICH paper and WHICH bytes — that is `MANIFEST.json` (sha256 + URL), ~10 KB.
#
# ⚠ Lanes read these by path (`pdfs/cordial-miners-shapiro-2205.09174.pdf`), so a
# fresh clone MUST run `scripts/fetch-papers.py` before any reader lane will work.
#
# The three FRI papers below predate this policy and are tracked; left alone
# rather than rewritten out of history.
*.pdf
!bciks20-proximity-gaps-2020-654.pdf
!improved-line-point-ldt-2311-12752.pdf
!kopparty-improved-rs-proximity-2025.pdf
